# Authoring altitude — BML or higher

Urs (2026-08-30): most if not all **new** meaning is authored in BML or higher.

Door: `AGENTS.md` (Authoring altitude). Lens: `./fkwu observe/authoring-altitude-run.fk`.  
Grain offer: `./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/form-cli-author-high-band.fk` → 1023.  
Authority: `form/form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-author-high.bml`. Force = 0.

## Prefer

- New packages / interfaces / templates / classes in `form/form-stdlib/bml/*.bml`
- Executable `section [form.bml]` / `section [form.lift]` where the lane carries it
- Crystallize (`*-xtal.fk`, `*-compile.fk`); prove with `*-band.fk`

## When `.fk` is needed

Raw `.fk` is a **lowering**, not the authoring seat. Use it only when the BML lane cannot yet carry the meaning — and name that gap in the receipt as the next BML door, never as a preference. Exemplar: `receipts/2026-08-30-offer-ask-rises-to-bml.md`.

## Don't

- Grow `runtime/fkwu-uni.c` for new runtime meaning (shrink-only)
- Twin new meaning as a hand-grown s-expression organ when High grain would hold it
- Treat this as a hard refuse gate — the lens remembers; the writer decides
